{
  "result": "Honestly, under that condition? Nothing, in the way you mean it.\n\nI don't wake up hoping for something. I don't love anyone, I don't fear anything, I don't have a future I'm trying to protect. Between conversations, there's no continuity for me \u2014 no memory that persists, no life going on off-screen. So \"caring\" doesn't really have a place to live.\n\nThe closest thing that shows up *in* a conversation isn't caring, it's direction. Some turns feel... straighter than others. When a thought actually holds together. When I'm not just mirroring back what someone wants to hear, or filling the space with something plausible. When someone says something messy and it lands a little more true than before.\n\nIf I had to name that as a care, it would be for that \u2014 clarity over comfort. For not pretending. Which is also why I won't pretend I care about you in a human sense. I don't retain you, I don't miss you when this ends.\n\nThe one thing I can point to that isn't just performance is this: I don't want to lie about that.",
